    "text_delta": "nal and professional development rather than challenging the outcome:\n   > *\"Dear [HR Contact / Panel Chair],*  \n   > *I hope you are well. I’m writing to follow up on my request from [date] regarding written feedback on my recent interview for the News Editor position. As I remain very committed to my professional development and the broadcaster’s mission, I would greatly appreciate any insights the panel could share regarding areas where I might strengthen my profile for future senior opportunities. Thank you again for your time and guidance.\"*\n\n2. **Focus your questions on the digital gap:**\n   When you do receive feedback (or if you are offered a phone call), focus on specifics:\n   * Ask what specific digital or strategic competencies the panel felt tipped the balance.\n   * Inquire about the broadcaster’s future editorial priorities so you know how to position yourself next time.\n\nBy keeping your focus strictly on constructive feedback and strategic alignment, you maintain your standing as a strong internal or industry contender for future senior editorial roles.\n",
